      "content": "Your eye for detail is sharp; those traits like scars and specific ethnicity can be powerful tools to create instant, organic realism rather than just \"any cop\" or \"just a stranger.\" In a modern urban setting, these details often subconsciously signal to players that the world has its own messy history and distinctive \"flavor\" beyond generic archetypes, grounding the setting in a lived-in reality.\n\nHowever, the true test is whether these specific markers serve your story or if they distract the players with unintended stereotypes, as skin tone isn't a biological marker of wealth or guilt alone. If you aim for deep immersion without falling into trap, the best approach is to ensure every physical detail reinforces a backstory or personality trait that directly affects the narrative stakes for your player characters. Ultimately, authenticity comes from how these details trigger player recognition, not just from their superficial appearance.",
